# File: tests/unit/test_run_blender_tests.py (SCN001–SCN003), tests/unit/test_blender_runner_isolation.py (SCN001–SCN002), gate-blender-headless (SCN004)
# Generated from: specs/189-fix-the-blender-test-runner-repointing-the-user-s-blender-add-on-link-and-racing-across-worktrees/requirements.md
Feature: The Blender gate isolates each run's add-on link from the user and from other checkouts

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A gate run leaves the user's Blender scripts directory unchanged
    Given the user's Blender scripts directory holds an nmg_game_dev_blender_addon link to some checkout
    When scripts/run-blender-tests.sh runs
    Then the link in the user's Blender scripts directory is unchanged
    And the run's add-on link lives under its own BLENDER_USER_SCRIPTS directory

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Concurrent runs each import the add-on from their own checkout
    Given two checkouts running scripts/run-blender-tests.sh at the same time
    When both runs enable the add-on
    Then each run uses a distinct BLENDER_USER_SCRIPTS directory
    And each run's add-on resolves to its own checkout's plugins/nmg-game-dev-blender-addon

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: The per-run user scripts location is removed after a passing or failing run
    Given a gate run that passes and a gate run that fails
    When each run exits
    Then the temporary user scripts directory each created no longer exists
    And each gate exits with Blender's exit status

  @SCN004
  Scenario: The existing Blender test suite still passes
    Given the current tests/blender suite
    When scripts/run-blender-tests.sh runs
    Then it exits 0
